(Kver - a keyboard-friendly PDF reader) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A keyboard-friendly PDF reader, starting on macOS.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Kver aims to be a responsive PDF reader for people who spend a lot of time) Tj T*
(reading documents. A single-page technical prototype exists; there is no) Tj T*
(downloadable reader yet.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The name Kver is Icelandic for a small book or booklet.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Inspired by Sioyek and Skim, Kver aims to pair keyboard navigation with a) Tj T*
(minimal desktop interface.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Although particularly suited to developers, researchers, and technical users,) Tj T*
(Kver aims to be a general-purpose PDF reader that is equally comfortable with) Tj T*
(a mouse.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Goals) Tj T*
(- Fast and responsive PDF viewing) Tj T*
(- Keyboard-first, but not keyboard-only) Tj T*
(- A first downloadable release on macOS, with Linux and Windows as separate) Tj T*
(  targets) Tj T*
(- Minimal, distraction-free interface) Tj T*
(- Powerful navigation inspired by Vim and Sioyek) Tj T*
(- Search, text interaction, and reading-position restoration as the reader) Tj T*
(  matures) Tj T*
(- A visual ruler and configurable keyboard shortcuts as future goals) Tj T*
